# A scene feature the shader exposes can be switched off while the program runs,
# and the prisoner counts follow it. ADR-0017.
#
# Two things are pinned here, and the second is the reason this is a decision
# rather than a keyword.
#
# 1. A capability is not a setting. `"bowls": 1` on a shader entry says the scene
#    *contains* the vessels; whether they are drawn is the user's. Only a shader
#    declaring the capability offers the parameters at all, which is why the
#    Minimal scenes below offer none rather than offering a toggle that would do
#    nothing.
#
# 2. The prisoners live in the LIDS, not the bowls. cc[0] and cc[1] are the lids
#    and bowl_stones.glsl fills them from iBlackCapturedCount /
#    iWhiteCapturedCount; the bowls hold the reservoir. So it is showLids that
#    PrisonerMode::Auto has to follow — a toggle wired to showBowls instead would
#    let someone hide the pile while Auto went on believing it was there, and the
#    captured stones would then be counted nowhere at all.
#
# NOT covered here, and it is where the first real bug was: persistence across a
# restart. run_scenarios.sh hands every scenario a throwaway user.json, so a
# value written by one run cannot be read by another. Verified by hand instead —
# the write was keyed by UserSettings::getShaderName(), which is empty until
# something saves the selection, while the read used the shader entry's own
# name. It persisted under "" and was never loaded back. Two identities for one
# object, which is the thing ADR-0017 decision 4 exists to forbid.

new_game 9
wait_idle

# Red Carpet is shader 0 and declares the capability, so both parameters are
# offered and both ship on.
expect shader_param_showBowls true
expect shader_param_showLids true

# Auto keeps the margin counts off, because the pile is visible.
prisoners auto
wait_idle
expect prisoner_mode auto
expect prisoner_shown false

# --- Switching the lids off brings the counts back --------------------------
shader_param showLids off
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showLids false
expect prisoner_shown true

# And back again. The setting is live: no relink, which is the whole point of a
# uniform bool over a #define (2019 ms cold, ADR-0013).
shader_param showLids on
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showLids true
expect prisoner_shown false

# --- The bowls are independent, and cost no information ---------------------
# Hiding the reservoir says nothing about the prisoners, so Auto must not react.
shader_param showBowls off
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showBowls false
expect shader_param_showLids true
expect prisoner_shown false

# `toggle` is accepted too, and reads the value in force rather than a copy.
shader_param showBowls toggle
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showBowls true

# --- The menu item, not just the command ------------------------------------
# The wiring nothing else covers: every step above dispatches a command
# directly, which is exactly how three selects once shipped with no branch to
# carry their value. Same hazard one level over, for the items that are clicked.
menu_click cmdParam_showLids
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showLids false
expect prisoner_shown true

menu_click cmdParam_showLids
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showLids true
expect prisoner_shown false

# --- A shader without the capability offers nothing -------------------------
# One step along the list is Minimal Thin, whose scene has no vessels at all.
# It contributes no shader_param_* keys, and the counts are shown because there
# is no pile anywhere.
cycle shaders
wait_idle
expect prisoner_shown true

# And the menu says so: the item is greyed, and greyed means it does not act.
# `pointer-events: none` keeps a real mouse off it; menu_click refuses for the
# same reason, or the harness could do what a user cannot.
#
# `prisoner_shown` alone would prove nothing here — it is true on this shader
# whatever happens, because there is no pile to hide. What the refusal has to
# not do is corrupt the value Red Carpet will come back to, so that is what is
# asserted, after cycling the rest of the way round the list (six shaders).
menu_click cmdParam_showLids
wait_idle
expect prisoner_shown true

cycle shaders
cycle shaders
cycle shaders
cycle shaders
cycle shaders
wait_idle
expect shader_param_showLids true
expect prisoner_shown false

# The explicit modes still outrank the shader, as ADR-0016 has it.
prisoners never
wait_idle
expect prisoner_shown false
